// REQUESTS 16: a tie on ONE member of a chord. LilyPond's chord_body takes '~' as a post-event
// of the member (<c'' f'' d'''~>8. <c'' f'' d'''>16: only the d''' is tied; see the .ly beside this),
// as Lily# already takes a slur mark on a member (<c e( g>4 <d f) a>). Today lysc rejects it:
//   <c'' f'' d'''~>8. <c'' f'' d'''>16   -> LYS0002 Expected 'CloseAngle', found 'Tilde'
// What the OMR reads: a held note on one stem with the inner voice's repeated chords (an old
// print, kinkel7-1's scan, bar 19: d'''4.~ d'''8 over <c'' f''>8 eighths). A '~' after the chord
// ties every note the next chord repeats, so the c'' and f'' would be tied too (bar 2 below).
// Bar 1: the chord's '~' to the same chord (all three tied: right where the print ties all).
// Bar 2: the chord's '~' where the print ties only the d''' -- the c'' and f'' tied are extra.
// Bar 3: the chord's '~' to a single note: only the d''' is tied (as LilyPond's tie-column), no warning.
// Bar 4 (commented out): the spelling asked for.
octave absolute
title "A chord member's tie"
time 3/4
key c major
part rh {
  clef treble
  section A {
    <c'' f'' d'''>8.~ <c'' f'' d'''>16 r2 |
    <c'' f'' d'''>8.~ <c'' f'' d'''>16 r2 |
    <c'' f'' d'''>8.~ d'''16 r2 |
    // <c'' f'' d'''~>8. <c'' f'' d'''>16 r2 |
  }
}
form { A }
score { staff rh }
